From 491f95dbb46e382c9aa84eb8da25049cfb4a06d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homar <homar@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:57:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] homalawn device profile: where the home screen really draws,
 for the desktop preview

New command launcher.device_profile (link and provider) reports the home
screen's geometry in screen pixels: the screen and its density, the system
bar insets, the grid, the workspace's grid of cells (position, cell size,
gaps), the icon size, label text size and icon-to-label padding and where
the icon sits in its cell, the dock's cells and icon size, the page
indicator and whether it shows, the folder icon size and widget padding.
It is measured from the launcher's laid-out views when there are any
(source: views), else summed from Lawnchair's DeviceProfile (source:
profile). The desktop's home-screen preview draws from these numbers.
